export const modernPerspective = [
  'In production electronic-structure calculations, crystallographic symmetry is inferred from finite-precision coordinates using numerical tolerances. A conventional cell, a primitive cell, and a symmetry-standardized cell may encode the same infinite crystal while using different vectors, origins, atom orderings, and reciprocal-space labels. These representational choices must be distinguished from a genuine structural change.',
  'A high-symmetry band path and a Brillouin-zone integration mesh answer different questions. A path is a one-dimensional visualization through selected k-space lines; total energies, densities, Fermi surfaces, and densities of states require sampling the full Brillouin zone. A pocket or extremum can therefore exist away from every plotted high-symmetry line.',
